# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz/short
msgid "9. Trajektorie péče"
msgstr "9. Care pathway"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz/definition
msgid "Logický model pro zachycení informací o klinické trajektorii (care pathway) pacienta v rámci péče o vzácné onemocnění. Obsahuje informace o odesílajícím subjektu, datu přijetí do specializovaného centra, zapojených lékařích a klinických službách."
msgstr "Patient care pathway across providers and specialist centres, including referral, inclusion dates, physicians and clinical services."

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway/short
msgid "Klinická trajektorie pacienta"
msgstr "Care pathway"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway/definition
msgid "Záznam o postupu péče pacienta napříč zdravotnickými subjekty a specializovanými centry."
msgstr "Patient care across healthcare providers and specialist centres."

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.odesilajiciSubjekt/short
msgid "Odesílající subjekt"
msgstr "9.1 Patient Referred By"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.odesilajiciSubjekt/definition
msgid "Identifikace odesílajícího subjektu (např. IČZ, typ poskytovatele, název)."
msgstr "The clinician or healthcare professional that referred the patient to the current (rare disease) centre (e.g., GP, another specialist physician), ideally coded via the healthcare professional’s professional identifier.\n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSHealthProfessional.identifier\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSHealthProfessional-definitions.html#key_EHDSHealthProfessional.identifier"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datumDoporuceni/short
msgid "Datum doporučení"
msgstr "9.2 Date of Referral"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datumDoporuceni/definition
msgid "Datum, kdy byl pacient doporučen k dalšímu vyšetření nebo péči."
msgstr "Date when referral was received by the treating (RD) centre. This information helps to assess wait times and access metrics.\n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSEncounter.plannedStartDate\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSEncounter-definitions.html#key_EHDSEncounter.plannedStartDate\n"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datumPrijetiSCentra/short
msgid "Datum přijetí do specializovaného centra"
msgstr "9.3 Date of Inclusion in RD Centre"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datumPrijetiSCentra/definition
msgid "Datum, kdy byl pacient přijat do specializovaného centra péče o vzácné onemocnění."
msgstr "Date when the patient was first formally registered or included in the rare disease centre’s cohort/system. This data element refers to the patient’s first inclusion and is only to be completed once and does not require updating.\nThis information helps to assess wait times and access metrics.\n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSEncounter.plannedStartDate\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSEncounter-definitions.html#key_EHDSEncounter.plannedStartDate\n"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.osetrujiciLekari/short
msgid "Jména ošetřujících lékařů"
msgstr "9.4 Names of Treating Physicians"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.osetrujiciLekari/definition
msgid "Seznam jmen lékařů zapojených do péče. Může zahrnovat garanta léčby, ošetřující lékaře apod. Možnost výběru z nabídky."
msgstr "Clinicians primarily responsible for the patient’s care (treating physician(s)).\n\nThis data element is Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSHealthProfessional.identifier\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSHealthProfessional-definitions.html#key_EHDSHealthProfessional.identifier\n\nAnd EHDSHealthProfessional.name\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSHealthProfessional-definitions.html#key_EHDSHealthProfessional.name\n"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datum/short
msgid "A.1.5.5 Datum a čas uložení"
msgstr "Date and time last saved"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.datum/definition
msgid "Datum a čas poslední modifikace dokumentu."
msgstr "Date and time of the last modification. An existing model extension beyond the source dataset."

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.centrumVzacnychOnemocneni/short
msgid "Centrum pro vzácná onemocnění"
msgstr "9.5 Rare Disease Centre"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.centrumVzacnychOnemocneni/definition
msgid "Název nebo kontakt na centrum péče o vzácná onemocnění. Vyplňuje se dle zadávající organizace."
msgstr "Name of the centre providing specialised rare disease care.\n\nThis data element is Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSHealthProfessional.professionalRole.organisation\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSHealthProfessional-definitions.html#key_EHDSHealthProfessional.professionalRole.organisation\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSOrganisation-definitions.html#key_EHDSOrganisation.address\n"

# A concise description of what this element means (e.g. for use in autogenerated summaries).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.klinickaSluzba/short
msgid "Klinická služba"
msgstr "9.6 Clinical Service"

# Provides a complete explanation of the meaning of the data element for human readability.  For the case of elements derived from existing elements (e.g. constraints), the definition SHALL be consistent with the base definition, but convey the meaning of the element in the particular context of use of the resource. (Note: The text you are reading is specified in ElementDefinition.definition).
#: StructureDefinition.element.LogCarePathwayCz.carePathway.klinickaSluzba/definition
msgid "Popis souvisejících klinických služeb – může se týkat kontaktu, vyšetření, ERN centra nebo konziliární služby. Nutné upřesnit období."
msgstr "Specific clinical unit / service within the centre responsible for providing care to the patient (e.g., cardiology unit, neuromuscular service etc).\n\nThis data element is Not Mandatory\n\nThe recommended data standard is EHDSHealthProfessional.professionalRole.specialty via SNOMED CT\n•\thttps://www.xt-ehr.eu/fhir/models/0.2.1/StructureDefinition-EHDSHealthProfessional-definitions.html#key_EHDSHealthProfessional.professionalRole.specialty\n"

